Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-01
Subject: Use ARM compiler-local bit helpers during tp2cc bootstrap
License: expat

The ARM compiler backend calls BsfDWord, BsrDWord, and SarLongint from the
RTL System unit.  During the tp2cc stage1 translation, compiler units are
translated as compiler units; the RTL System helper implementations are not in
that unit graph.  Keep the ARM backend's intended bit operations local to the
ARM compiler unit instead.

--- a/compiler/arm/aoptcpu.pas
+++ b/compiler/arm/aoptcpu.pas
@@ -1033,7 +1033,7 @@
                            (taicpu(hp1).oper[2]^.typ = top_const) and
                            { Check if the BIC actually would only mask out bits beeing already zero because of the shift }
                            (taicpu(hp1).oper[2]^.val<>0) and
-                           (BsfDWord(taicpu(hp1).oper[2]^.val)>=32-taicpu(p).oper[2]^.shifterop^.shiftimm) then
+                           (arm_bsf_dword(taicpu(hp1).oper[2]^.val)>=32-taicpu(p).oper[2]^.shifterop^.shiftimm) then
                            begin
                              DebugMsg('Peephole LsrBic2Lsr done', hp1);
                              taicpu(p).oper[0]^.reg:=taicpu(hp1).oper[0]^.reg;
